IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpq13a-dates`

-- Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland), Part 13A (ss 103A-103ZC) and s 111 -- representative proceedings (class
-- actions) in the Supreme Court, as the PERSON WITH A CLAIM meets them.
--
-- SEAT: an individual who has a claim against a defendant that is, or could be, pursued in a representative
-- proceeding: usually a group member (one of the people on whose behalf the proceeding is brought), and, for the
-- questions marked so, the representative party (the group member who starts it and runs it for the others). "Can a
-- class action be brought for my claim?", "Am I in the group?", "By when can I opt out?", "Is my time to sue running?",
-- "Am I bound by the judgment?", "Can I be made to pay costs?", "By when must I claim from the fund?", "Can I appeal if
-- the representative party does not?". The defendant meets the same rules from the other side; the court gets no seat.
-- Every power of the court is answered conditionally: the court's view is asked as a fact, never decided.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list). Four time limits are
-- DEONTIC rules run inside (opting out, claiming from a fund, a group member's appeal, suing once the limitation period
-- runs again); no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Proceedings Act 2011, Part 13A: the questions of a person with a claim in a representative proceeding`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `The parties, the acts and the time rules`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103A: "representative party means a person who starts a representative proceeding"; "group member means a member
-- of a group of persons on whose behalf a representative proceeding has been started"; "defendant means a person
-- against whom relief is sought in a representative proceeding"; "court means the Supreme Court".
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `I`
    `the representative party`

DECLARE `Act done` IS ONE OF
    `give written notice that I opt out`
    `make a claim for payment from the fund`
    `start an appeal`
    `start my own proceeding`

-- Runs a rule for me over one act done at a time counted in days from the rule's start. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on
-- an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH. It takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
      `the act` IS AN `Act done`
      `the time it was done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `done in time under` `the rule` `the act` `at` `the time it was done` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time it was done`), (EVENT `I` `the act` `the time it was done`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103B, 103C, 103F, 111 -- starting a representative proceeding`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 111(1) "Part 13A applies only to a proceeding started after the commencement." (2) "The proceeding may be started
-- even if the cause of action the subject of the proceeding arose before the commencement." The commencement of the
-- Limitation of Actions (Child Sexual Abuse) and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2016 is not in the deposited text: it is
-- asked as a yes/no fact (fork F1). Closed with "only": JUST FALSE kind.
--
-- s 103B(1) "A proceeding may be started under this part if-- (a) 7 or more persons have claims against the same
-- person; and (b) the claims of all the persons are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related
-- circumstances; and (c) the claims of all the persons give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact." A
-- condition introduced by "if": JUST FALSE kind when a limb fails. Whether circumstances are related and whether an
-- issue is substantial and common are, in the end, for the court: asked (fork F2). s 103B(3) (relief that is equitable,
-- damages, individually assessed damages or different for each person; separate contracts, transactions, acts or
-- omissions) says these do not stop a proceeding: no input is needed for them.
DECLARE `Can a representative proceeding be started` IS ONE OF
    `yes: 7 or more persons have claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances and giving rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 103B(1)); 1 or more of them may start it for some or all of the others (s 103B(2))`
    `no: Part 13A applies only to a proceeding started after it commenced (s 111(1))`
    `no: fewer than 7 persons have claims against the same person (s 103B(1)(a))`
    `no: the claims do not all arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances (s 103B(1)(b))`
    `no: the claims do not all give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 103B(1)(c))`

GIVEN `after commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons` IS A NUMBER
      `related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Can a representative proceeding be started`
`ss 103B(1), 111 -- a representative proceeding may be started` `after commencement` `the number of persons` `related circumstances` `substantial common issue` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`after commencement`)
        THEN `no: Part 13A applies only to a proceeding started after it commenced (s 111(1))`
        IF `the number of persons` LESS THAN 7
        THEN `no: fewer than 7 persons have claims against the same person (s 103B(1)(a))`
        IF NOT (`related circumstances`)
        THEN `no: the claims do not all arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances (s 103B(1)(b))`
        IF NOT (`substantial common issue`)
        THEN `no: the claims do not all give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 103B(1)(c))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: 7 or more persons have claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances and giving rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 103B(1)); 1 or more of them may start it for some or all of the others (s 103B(2))`

GIVEN `after commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons` IS A NUMBER
      `related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103B(1) is met` `after commencement` `the number of persons` `related circumstances` `substantial common issue` IF
    `ss 103B(1), 111 -- a representative proceeding may be started` `after commencement` `the number of persons` `related circumstances` `substantial common issue` EQUALS `yes: 7 or more persons have claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances and giving rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (s 103B(1)); 1 or more of them may start it for some or all of the others (s 103B(2))`

@export Can a representative proceeding (a class action) be started in the Queensland Supreme Court for my claim and the claims of others against the same person, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 Part 13A (s 103B, s 111)? It needs 7 or more persons with claims against the same person, arising out of the same, similar or related circumstances, and giving rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact. It does not matter that damages must be assessed person by person, or that each person had a separate contract or dealing with the defendant.
GIVEN `after commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceeding is (or would be) started after Part 13A commenced (it was inserted by the Limitation of Actions (Child Sexual Abuse) and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2016); the cause of action may have arisen earlier
      `the number of persons` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons, you included, have claims against the same person (the proposed defendant)
      `related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the claims are in respect of, or arise out of, the same, similar or related circumstances (in the end the court's view)
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the claims give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (in the end the court's view)
GIVETH A `Can a representative proceeding be started`
`Can a representative proceeding be started for my claim` MEANS
    `ss 103B(1), 111 -- a representative proceeding may be started` `after commencement` `the number of persons` `related circumstances` `substantial common issue`

-- s 103C(1) "A person who has a claim as mentioned in section 103B(1)(a) has a sufficient interest to start a
-- representative proceeding against another person (the proposed defendant) on behalf of other persons who also have a
-- claim as mentioned in that section if the person has standing to start proceedings on the person's own behalf against
-- the proposed defendant." (2) more than 1 defendant, whether or not each person has a claim against each. A condition
-- introduced by "if": JUST FALSE kind (fork F3).
DECLARE `Can I start it` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may start it, as the representative party, on behalf of the others (ss 103B(2), 103C(1)); against more than 1 defendant if you wish, even if not every group member has a claim against each (s 103C(2))`
    `no: a representative proceeding cannot be started for these claims (s 103B(1) or s 111)`
    `no: you need a claim of your own against the proposed defendant, as one of the 7 or more (s 103C(1))`
    `no: you need standing to start a proceeding on your own behalf against the proposed defendant (s 103C(1))`

@export Can I start a representative proceeding (class action) myself, as the representative party, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) ss 103B and 103C? A person with one of the claims has a sufficient interest to start it on behalf of the others if they could sue the defendant on their own behalf.
GIVEN `after commencement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceeding would be started after Part 13A commenced (it was inserted by the Limitation of Actions (Child Sexual Abuse) and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2016)
      `the number of persons` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons, you included, have claims against the same person (the proposed defendant)
      `related circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances (in the end the court's view)
      `substantial common issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the claims give rise to a substantial common issue of law or fact (in the end the court's view)
      `I have a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you yourself have a claim against the proposed defendant, as one of those persons
      `I have standing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have standing to start a proceeding on your own behalf against the proposed defendant
GIVETH A `Can I start it`
`Can I start a representative proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 103B(1) is met` `after commencement` `the number of persons` `related circumstances` `substantial common issue`)
        THEN `no: a representative proceeding cannot be started for these claims (s 103B(1) or s 111)`
        IF NOT (`I have a claim`)
        THEN `no: you need a claim of your own against the proposed defendant, as one of the 7 or more (s 103C(1))`
        IF NOT (`I have standing`)
        THEN `no: you need standing to start a proceeding on your own behalf against the proposed defendant (s 103C(1))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you may start it, as the representative party, on behalf of the others (ss 103B(2), 103C(1)); against more than 1 defendant if you wish, even if not every group member has a claim against each (s 103C(2))`

-- s 103C(3) "A person who has started a representative proceeding retains standing to do the following even if the
-- person ceases to have a claim against any or all defendants-- (a) continue the proceeding; (b) appeal against a
-- decision in the proceeding." For a person who did not start it (a representative party substituted under s 103P or
-- s 103S(3)) whose claim has ended, the subsection is silent: NOTHING (fork F4).
@export As the representative party, can I carry on the representative proceeding, or appeal a decision in it, after my own claim against the defendant (or every defendant) has ended, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103C(3)?
GIVEN `I started it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the person who started the representative proceeding (answer no if you became representative party later, by substitution)
      `my claim has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you no longer have a claim against any or all of the defendants (for example because you settled your own claim)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I carry on after my own claim ends` MEANS
    IF `I started it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `my claim has ended`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 103F(1) "The originating process ... must ... (a) describe or otherwise identify the group members ...; (b) state
-- the nature of the claims made and relief sought ...; (c) state the questions of law or fact common to the claims".
-- (2) it is not necessary to name or state the number of the group members. A "must": JUST FALSE when a limb is missing.
@export As the representative party, does my originating process (or a document filed in support of it) contain what the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103F requires? It must describe or otherwise identify the group members, state the nature of the claims and the relief sought for them, and state the common questions of law or fact. It need not name the group members or say how many there are.
GIVEN `identifies the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it describes or otherwise identifies the group members to whom the proceeding relates (names and numbers are not needed)
      `states claims and relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the nature of the claims made and the relief sought on behalf of the group members
      `states common questions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the questions of law or fact common to the claims of the group members
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my originating process meet s 103F` MEANS
    IF `identifies the group` AND `states claims and relief` AND `states common questions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103A, 103D, 103E -- being a group member`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103D(1) "Subject to subsection (2), the consent of a person to be a group member is not required." (2) the
-- Commonwealth or a State; a Minister; a body corporate established for a public purpose by a law of the Commonwealth or
-- a State, other than an incorporated company or association; an officer, in that capacity -- "is a group member only if
-- the person gives consent in writing". Closed with "only if": JUST FALSE kind.
DECLARE `Who I am` IS ONE OF
    `a private person, company or other body`
    `the Commonwealth or a State`
    `a Minister of the Commonwealth or a State`
    `a body corporate established for a public purpose by a law of the Commonwealth or a State (not an incorporated company or association)`
    `an officer of the Commonwealth or a State, acting in that capacity`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who I am`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103D(2) -- consent in writing is required` `who` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `a private person, company or other body` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 103A "group member means a member of a group of persons on whose behalf a representative proceeding has been
-- started" (a "means" definition), the group being the one the originating process describes (s 103F(1)(a), as amended
-- under s 103H). A person who has opted out under s 103G is taken to be no longer a group member (fork F5).
DECLARE `Am I a group member` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are within the description of the group, and your consent is not needed (s 103D(1))`
    `yes: you are within the description of the group and have consented in writing (s 103D(2))`
    `no: you are not within the description of the group members in the originating process (s 103A, s 103F(1)(a))`
    `no: as the Commonwealth, a State, a Minister, a public body or an officer, you are a group member only if you consent in writing (s 103D(2))`
    `no: you have opted out (s 103G)`

@export Am I a group member of a representative proceeding (class action) in the Queensland Supreme Court, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 Part 13A (ss 103A, 103D, 103G)? A person within the description of the group in the originating process is a group member without having to consent, unless they have opted out; only the Commonwealth, a State, a Minister, a public body or an officer must consent in writing.
GIVEN `within the description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you fall within the description of the group members in the originating process (as amended, if it has been)
      `who` IS A `Who I am` @desc What you are: "a private person, company or other body" for nearly everyone; otherwise the Commonwealth or a State, a Minister, a public-purpose body corporate, or an officer acting as such
      `consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given your consent in writing to be a group member (needed only by the Commonwealth, a State, a Minister, a public body or an officer)
      `opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have opted out of the proceeding by written notice before the date the court fixed
GIVETH A `Am I a group member`
`Am I a group member` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`within the description`)
        THEN `no: you are not within the description of the group members in the originating process (s 103A, s 103F(1)(a))`
        IF `opted out`
        THEN `no: you have opted out (s 103G)`
        IF NOT (`s 103D(2) -- consent in writing is required` `who`)
        THEN `yes: you are within the description of the group, and your consent is not needed (s 103D(1))`
        IF `consented in writing`
        THEN `yes: you are within the description of the group and have consented in writing (s 103D(2))`
        OTHERWISE `no: as the Commonwealth, a State, a Minister, a public body or an officer, you are a group member only if you consent in writing (s 103D(2))`

-- s 103E(1) "It is not necessary for a person under a legal incapacity to have a litigation guardian merely in order to
-- be a group member." (2) "A group member who is a person under a legal incapacity may only take a step in the
-- representative proceeding or conduct part of the proceeding by the member's litigation guardian." "Person under a
-- legal incapacity" is borrowed from the Supreme Court of Queensland Act 1991 (not deposited): asked.
DECLARE `What I want to do` IS ONE OF
    `just be a group member`
    `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it`

DECLARE `Do I need a litigation guardian` IS ONE OF
    `no: a person under a legal incapacity does not need a litigation guardian merely to be a group member (s 103E(1))`
    `yes: as a group member under a legal incapacity you may take a step or conduct part of the proceeding only by your litigation guardian (s 103E(2))`
    `not covered: s 103E is only about persons under a legal incapacity`

@export As a group member under a legal incapacity (for example a child or an adult with impaired capacity), do I need a litigation guardian, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103E?
GIVEN `under a legal incapacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person under a legal incapacity, as the Supreme Court of Queensland Act 1991 defines it (for example a child, or an adult with impaired capacity)
      `what` IS A `What I want to do` @desc Whether you only want to be a group member, or want to take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it
GIVETH A `Do I need a litigation guardian`
`Do I need a litigation guardian` MEANS
    IF NOT (`under a legal incapacity`)
    THEN `not covered: s 103E is only about persons under a legal incapacity`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what`
         WHEN `just be a group member` THEN `no: a person under a legal incapacity does not need a litigation guardian merely to be a group member (s 103E(1))`
         WHEN `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it` THEN `yes: as a group member under a legal incapacity you may take a step or conduct part of the proceeding only by your litigation guardian (s 103E(2))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103G -- opting out` -- situation: you have been told of a representative proceeding that includes you
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103G(1) "The court must fix a date before which a group member may opt out". (2) "A group member may opt out ... by
-- giving written notice before the date fixed under subsection (1)." (3) the court may fix a later date. "Before the
-- date": the last day is the day before it (fork F6).
GIVEN `the date fixed` IS A DATE, `a later date was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the later date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 103G -- the opt-out date` `the date fixed` `a later date was fixed` `the later date` MEANS
    IF `a later date was fixed` THEN `the later date` ELSE `the date fixed`

-- The rule: I DO give written notice WITHIN the days from the start of the proceeding to the day before the date. The
-- BREACH marks only that I did not opt out in time (and so stay a group member, bound by the judgment, s 103X): not
-- opting out is not a wrong.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 103G -- opt out by written notice before the date fixed` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `give written notice that I opt out`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "no written notice before the date the court fixed: the person stays a group member and is bound by the judgment (ss 103G, 103X)"

DECLARE `Have I opted out` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you opted out by written notice before the date the court fixed (s 103G(2))`
    `no: you have not given written notice of opting out (s 103G(2))`
    `no: your notice was given on or after the date the court fixed for opting out (s 103G(2)); the court may fix a later date on an application (s 103G(3))`
    `not covered: your notice was given before the representative proceeding started`

@export Have I opted out of the representative proceeding in time, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103G? A group member opts out by giving written notice before the date the court fixes (or a later date the court fixes on an application by a group member, the representative party or the defendant).
GIVEN `the day it started` IS A DATE @desc The day the representative proceeding was started (ISO 8601, e.g. 2027-03-01)
      `the date fixed` IS A DATE @desc The date the court fixed, before which group members may opt out (from the notice you were given)
      `a later date was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has since fixed a later date for opting out
      `the later date` IS A DATE @desc The later date the court fixed (any date if none was fixed)
      `I gave written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave written notice that you opt out
      `the day I gave it` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the written notice (any date if you gave none)
GIVETH A `Have I opted out`
`Have I opted out in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`I gave written notice`)
        THEN `no: you have not given written notice of opting out (s 103G(2))`
        IF `the day` `the day I gave it` `is before` `the day it started`
        THEN `not covered: your notice was given before the representative proceeding started`
        IF `done in time under` (`s 103G -- opt out by written notice before the date fixed` (`the days from` `the day it started` `to` (`the day before` (`s 103G -- the opt-out date` `the date fixed` `a later date was fixed` `the later date`)))) `give written notice that I opt out` `at` (`the days from` `the day it started` `to` `the day I gave it`)
        THEN `yes: you opted out by written notice before the date the court fixed (s 103G(2))`
        OTHERWISE `no: your notice was given on or after the date the court fixed for opting out (s 103G(2)); the court may fix a later date on an application (s 103G(3))`

@export What is the last day on which I can give written notice opting out of the representative proceeding, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103G? The notice must be given before the date the court fixed (or a later date it has fixed), so the last day is the day before that date.
GIVEN `the date fixed` IS A DATE @desc The date the court fixed, before which group members may opt out (ISO 8601)
      `a later date was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has since fixed a later date for opting out
      `the later date` IS A DATE @desc The later date the court fixed (any date if none was fixed)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day I can opt out` MEANS
    `the day before` (`s 103G -- the opt-out date` `the date fixed` `a later date was fixed` `the later date`)

-- s 103G(4) "Except by leave of the court, the hearing of a representative proceeding must not start earlier than the
-- date before which a group member may opt out of the proceeding." A flat negative: JUST FALSE kind.
@export Can the hearing of the representative proceeding start before the date for opting out, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103G(4)? Only with the court's leave.
GIVEN `the date fixed` IS A DATE @desc The date before which group members may opt out (as fixed, or as later fixed, by the court)
      `the hearing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the hearing starts or is listed to start
      `leave given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given leave for the hearing to start earlier
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the hearing start before the opt-out date` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day` `the hearing day` `is before` `the date fixed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `leave given`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103H -- joining the group when your cause of action accrued later`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103H(1) on the representative party's application the court may give leave to amend the description of the group;
-- (2) to include a person "(a) whose cause of action accrued after the start of the representative proceeding but before
-- the date fixed by the court when giving leave; and (b) who would have been a group member or, with the consent of the
-- person would have been a group member, if the cause of action had accrued before the proceeding was started". A grant
-- ("may be changed to include") limited in its own words, with no "only": outside the limit NOTHING kind ("not covered
-- by s 103H"), per the scope-limit ruling (fork F7).
DECLARE `Can I be added under s 103H` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court has given leave, and the description of the group may be changed to include you (s 103H(1), (2))`
    `possibly: you qualify under s 103H(2); the representative party may apply for leave to change the description of the group to include you, and the court decides`
    `not covered by s 103H: your cause of action did not accrue after the proceeding started (you may already be within the description of the group)`
    `not covered by s 103H: your cause of action accrued on or after the date the court fixed when giving leave (s 103H(2)(a))`
    `not covered by s 103H: you would not have been a group member even if your cause of action had accrued before the proceeding started (s 103H(2)(b))`

@export My cause of action accrued after the representative proceeding started. Can the group be changed to include me, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103H? On the representative party's application the court may give leave to change the description of the group to include persons whose cause of action accrued after the start but before a date the court fixes, and who would otherwise have been group members.
GIVEN `the day it started` IS A DATE @desc The day the representative proceeding was started (ISO 8601)
      `the day my cause accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action accrued
      `would have been a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would have been a group member (or would have been, with your consent) had your cause of action accrued before the proceeding started
      `leave given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given leave, on the representative party's application, to change the description of the group to include persons like you
      `the date fixed` IS A DATE @desc The date the court fixed when giving leave, before which a cause of action must have accrued (any date if no leave has been given)
GIVETH A `Can I be added under s 103H`
`Can I be added to the group after my cause accrued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the day` `the day it started` `is before` `the day my cause accrued`)
        THEN `not covered by s 103H: your cause of action did not accrue after the proceeding started (you may already be within the description of the group)`
        IF NOT (`would have been a member`)
        THEN `not covered by s 103H: you would not have been a group member even if your cause of action had accrued before the proceeding started (s 103H(2)(b))`
        IF NOT (`leave given`)
        THEN `possibly: you qualify under s 103H(2); the representative party may apply for leave to change the description of the group to include you, and the court decides`
        IF `the day` `the day my cause accrued` `is before` `the date fixed`
        THEN `yes: the court has given leave, and the description of the group may be changed to include you (s 103H(1), (2))`
        OTHERWISE `not covered by s 103H: your cause of action accrued on or after the date the court fixed when giving leave (s 103H(2)(a))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103Z -- your limitation period while the representative proceeding runs`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103Z(1) "On the starting of a representative proceeding, the running of any limitation period applying to the claim
-- of a group member to which the proceeding relates is suspended." (2) "The limitation period does not start running
-- again unless-- (a) the member opts out ... under section 103G; or (b) the representative proceeding, and any appeal
-- from the proceeding, is decided without finally disposing of the member's claim." (3) despite the Limitation of
-- Actions Act 1974 or any other law. "Unless": a flat no while neither event has happened. An order that the proceeding
-- no longer continue under Part 13A (ss 103I-103K), and a settlement or discontinuance approved under s 103R, are not
-- named: NOTHING kind (fork F8, finding 2).
DECLARE `What has happened to the proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `it is still going`
    `I opted out under s 103G`
    `it and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of my claim`
    `it and any appeal were decided, finally disposing of my claim`
    `the court ordered that it no longer continue under Part 13A`
    `it was settled or discontinued with the court's approval`

DECLARE `Is my limitation period suspended` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the limitation period for your claim stopped running when the representative proceeding started, and has not started again (s 103Z(1), (2))`
    `no, it is running again: you opted out (s 103Z(2)(a))`
    `no, it is running again: the proceeding and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of your claim (s 103Z(2)(b))`
    `not needed: your claim has been finally disposed of in the representative proceeding`
    `not covered: s 103Z(2) does not say whether the period runs again after an order that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A, or after an approved settlement or discontinuance`
    `not covered: s 103Z applies to the claim of a group member to which the proceeding relates`

GIVEN `a group member` IS A BOOLEAN, `what happened` IS A `What has happened to the proceeding`
GIVETH A `Is my limitation period suspended`
`s 103Z -- the suspension` `a group member` `what happened` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a group member`)
    THEN `not covered: s 103Z applies to the claim of a group member to which the proceeding relates`
    ELSE CONSIDER `what happened`
         WHEN `it is still going` THEN `yes: the limitation period for your claim stopped running when the representative proceeding started, and has not started again (s 103Z(1), (2))`
         WHEN `I opted out under s 103G` THEN `no, it is running again: you opted out (s 103Z(2)(a))`
         WHEN `it and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of my claim` THEN `no, it is running again: the proceeding and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of your claim (s 103Z(2)(b))`
         WHEN `it and any appeal were decided, finally disposing of my claim` THEN `not needed: your claim has been finally disposed of in the representative proceeding`
         WHEN `the court ordered that it no longer continue under Part 13A` THEN `not covered: s 103Z(2) does not say whether the period runs again after an order that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A, or after an approved settlement or discontinuance`
         WHEN `it was settled or discontinued with the court's approval` THEN `not covered: s 103Z(2) does not say whether the period runs again after an order that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A, or after an approved settlement or discontinuance`

@export Is the limitation period (the time limit to sue) for my claim suspended because a representative proceeding (class action) for it has started, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103Z? The period stops running when the proceeding starts, and starts again only if you opt out, or if the proceeding and any appeal are decided without finally disposing of your claim.
GIVEN `a group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are (or were, until you opted out) a group member, and your claim is one the representative proceeding relates to
      `what happened` IS A `What has happened to the proceeding` @desc Where the representative proceeding stands for you now
GIVETH A `Is my limitation period suspended`
`Is my limitation period suspended` MEANS
    `s 103Z -- the suspension` `a group member` `what happened`

-- The days of the period left when it was suspended: from the day the proceeding started to the last day the period
-- would otherwise have had (the starting day counted as used). The period starts running again on the day of the event
-- in s 103Z(2), and its last day is that day plus the days left (fork F8). If the proceeding started after the period had
-- already ended, nothing was left to suspend: the old last day stands.
GIVEN `the old last day` IS A DATE, `the day it started` IS A DATE, `the day it runs again` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 103Z -- the new last day` `the old last day` `the day it started` `the day it runs again` MEANS
    IF `the day` `the old last day` `is before` `the day it started`
    THEN `the old last day`
    ELSE `the day` (`the days from` `the day it started` `to` `the old last day`) `days after` `the day it runs again`

GIVEN `a group member` IS A BOOLEAN, `what happened` IS A `What has happened to the proceeding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103Z -- running again` `a group member` `what happened` IF
        (`s 103Z -- the suspension` `a group member` `what happened` EQUALS `no, it is running again: you opted out (s 103Z(2)(a))`)
    OR  (`s 103Z -- the suspension` `a group member` `what happened` EQUALS `no, it is running again: the proceeding and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of your claim (s 103Z(2)(b))`)

@export If my limitation period has started running again after a representative proceeding (because I opted out, or the proceeding ended without finally deciding my claim), by when must I start my own proceeding, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103Z? The days of the period that were left when the representative proceeding started are counted again from the day the period runs again. No date is given while the period is still suspended.
GIVEN `the old last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day for starting your own proceeding under the limitation period that applies to your claim (for example under the Limitation of Actions Act 1974), leaving the representative proceeding out of account (ISO 8601)
      `the day it started` IS A DATE @desc The day the representative proceeding was started
      `a group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are (or were, until you opted out) a group member, and your claim is one the representative proceeding relates to
      `what happened` IS A `What has happened to the proceeding` @desc Where the representative proceeding stands for you now
      `the day it runs again` IS A DATE @desc The day you opted out, or the day the proceeding and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of your claim (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I start my own proceeding` MEANS
    IF `s 103Z -- running again` `a group member` `what happened`
    THEN JUST (`s 103Z -- the new last day` `the old last day` `the day it started` `the day it runs again`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The rule: once the period runs again, I DO start my own proceeding WITHIN the days left. Not starting is not a wrong:
-- the BREACH marks only that the limitation period has run out.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 103Z -- start my own proceeding within the days left` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `start my own proceeding`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "the limitation period, suspended under s 103Z while the representative proceeding ran, has run out"

DECLARE `Am I in time to sue on my own` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you start within the limitation period, counting the suspension under s 103Z`
    `no: the limitation period has run out, even counting the suspension under s 103Z`
    `no need to count: the limitation period is still suspended (s 103Z(1), (2))`
    `not covered: s 103Z does not decide this (ask whether your limitation period is suspended)`

@export Am I in time to start my own proceeding on the day I plan to, counting the suspension of my limitation period while the representative proceeding ran, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103Z?
GIVEN `the old last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day for starting your own proceeding under the limitation period that applies to your claim, leaving the representative proceeding out of account (ISO 8601)
      `the day it started` IS A DATE @desc The day the representative proceeding was started
      `a group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are (or were, until you opted out) a group member, and your claim is one the representative proceeding relates to
      `what happened` IS A `What has happened to the proceeding` @desc Where the representative proceeding stands for you now
      `the day it runs again` IS A DATE @desc The day you opted out, or the day the proceeding and any appeal were decided without finally disposing of your claim (any date otherwise)
      `the day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you start, or plan to start, your own proceeding
GIVETH A `Am I in time to sue on my own`
`Am I in time to start my own proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`a group member`) AND (`what happened` EQUALS `it is still going`)
        THEN `no need to count: the limitation period is still suspended (s 103Z(1), (2))`
        IF NOT (`s 103Z -- running again` `a group member` `what happened`)
        THEN `not covered: s 103Z does not decide this (ask whether your limitation period is suspended)`
        IF `the day` `the day I start` `is before` `the day it runs again`
        THEN IF (`the day` `the day it started` `is on or before` `the old last day`) OR (`the day` `the day I start` `is on or before` `the old last day`)
             THEN `yes: you start within the limitation period, counting the suspension under s 103Z`
             ELSE `no: the limitation period has run out, even counting the suspension under s 103Z`
        IF `done in time under` (`s 103Z -- start my own proceeding within the days left` (`the days from` `the day it runs again` `to` (`s 103Z -- the new last day` `the old last day` `the day it started` `the day it runs again`))) `start my own proceeding` `at` (`the days from` `the day it runs again` `to` `the day I start`)
        THEN `yes: you start within the limitation period, counting the suspension under s 103Z`
        OTHERWISE `no: the limitation period has run out, even counting the suspension under s 103Z`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103V, 103W, 103X, 103U(8) -- judgment, damages and the fund` -- situation: the proceeding has been decided
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103X "A judgment given in a representative proceeding-- (a) must describe or otherwise identify the group members
-- affected by it; and (b) binds the group members described, other than a person who has opted out of the proceeding
-- under section 103G." s 103U(8) "The failure of a group member to receive or respond to a notice does not affect a
-- step taken, an order made, or a judgment given in the representative proceeding." "Other than" a person who opted out:
-- JUST FALSE (fork F10). A person the judgment does not describe: the section is silent, NOTHING.
@export Am I bound by the judgment in the representative proceeding (class action), under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103X? A judgment binds the group members it describes, except a person who opted out. Not receiving, or not answering, a notice in the proceeding does not change this (s 103U(8)).
GIVEN `described in the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judgment describes or otherwise identifies group members in a way that includes you
      `opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you opted out of the proceeding by written notice before the date the court fixed (s 103G)
      `I received the notices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received the notices given in the proceeding (it makes no difference, s 103U(8))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I bound by the judgment` MEANS
    IF `opted out`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `described in the judgment`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 103V(1)(f) the court may "award damages in an aggregate amount without stating amounts awarded in respect of
-- individual group members"; (3) "Other than as provided under section 103R, the court must not make an award of
-- damages as mentioned in subsection (1)(f) unless a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount to
-- which group members are entitled under the judgment." A flat negative with "unless": JUST FALSE kind. Whether an
-- assessment can be made is the court's view: asked.
DECLARE `Can damages be awarded as one total` IS ONE OF
    `yes, the court may award damages in an aggregate amount: a reasonably accurate assessment of the total can be made (s 103V(1)(f), (3))`
    `yes, the court may: the aggregate amount comes with a settlement approved under s 103R, to which s 103V(3) does not apply`
    `no: the court must not award damages in an aggregate amount unless a reasonably accurate assessment of the total can be made (s 103V(3))`

@export Can the court award damages to the group as one total amount, without saying what each group member gets, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103V? Only if a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total the group members are entitled to (or as part of a settlement the court approves).
GIVEN `under a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount is part of a settlement or discontinuance approved by the court under s 103R
      `total can be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a reasonably accurate assessment can be made of the total amount group members are entitled to under the judgment (in the end the court's view)
GIVETH A `Can damages be awarded as one total`
`Can damages be awarded as one total` MEANS
    IF `under a settlement`
    THEN `yes, the court may: the aggregate amount comes with a settlement approved under s 103R, to which s 103V(3) does not apply`
    ELSE IF `total can be assessed`
         THEN `yes, the court may award damages in an aggregate amount: a reasonably accurate assessment of the total can be made (s 103V(1)(f), (3))`
         ELSE `no: the court must not award damages in an aggregate amount unless a reasonably accurate assessment of the total can be made (s 103V(3))`

-- s 103W(3)(c) a fund order must "state a date, at least 6 months after the date on which the order is made, before
-- which the group members must make a claim for payment from the fund". "At least 6 months after": the date 6 months on
-- is enough (fork F9).
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE, `the date stated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103W(3)(c) -- at least 6 months after the order` `the day of the order` `the date stated` IF
    `the day` (`the date` 6 `months after` `the day of the order`) `is on or before` `the date stated`

@export Does the date the fund order gives for making claims meet the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103W(3)(c)? It must be at least 6 months after the day the order is made.
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day the court made the order constituting the fund (ISO 8601)
      `the date stated` IS A DATE @desc The date the order states, before which group members must claim from the fund
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the fund claim date meet s 103W` MEANS
    IF `s 103W(3)(c) -- at least 6 months after the order` `the day of the order` `the date stated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 103W(3)(b), (c): the group member "must make a claim for payment from the fund" before the date stated, in the way the
-- order states. (4) "The court may, if it considers it just, allow a group member to make a claim after the date stated
-- under subsection (3)(c) if the fund has not been fully distributed." The rule: I DO make the claim WITHIN the days from
-- the order to the day before the date stated. The BREACH marks only a late claim; (4) is answered outside the rule.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 103W -- claim from the fund before the date stated` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I`
    DO `make a claim for payment from the fund`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "no claim before the date stated in the fund order (s 103W(3)(c)); a late claim needs the court's leave while the fund is not fully distributed (s 103W(4))"

DECLARE `Am I in time to claim from the fund` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you claim before the date stated in the order (s 103W(3)(c))`
    `yes, late: the court has allowed you to claim after the date, the fund not being fully distributed (s 103W(4))`
    `late: the court may allow a late claim if it considers it just, while the fund is not fully distributed (s 103W(4)); it has not yet done so`
    `no: your claim is late and the fund has been fully distributed (s 103W(4))`

@export Am I in time to claim my share from the fund the court set up for the group members, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103W? A claim must be made before the date the fund order states; after it, the court may allow a late claim if it considers it just and the fund has not been fully distributed.
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE @desc The day the court made the order constituting the fund (ISO 8601)
      `the date stated` IS A DATE @desc The date the order states, before which group members must claim from the fund
      `the day I claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or plan to make) your claim, in the way the order states
      `fully distributed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fund has already been fully distributed
      `late claim allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has allowed you to make a claim after the date stated
GIVETH A `Am I in time to claim from the fund`
`Am I in time to claim from the fund` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `done in time under` (`s 103W -- claim from the fund before the date stated` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` (`the day before` `the date stated`))) `make a claim for payment from the fund` `at` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `the day I claim`)
        THEN `yes: you claim before the date stated in the order (s 103W(3)(c))`
        IF `fully distributed`
        THEN `no: your claim is late and the fund has been fully distributed (s 103W(4))`
        IF `late claim allowed`
        THEN `yes, late: the court has allowed you to claim after the date, the fund not being fully distributed (s 103W(4))`
        OTHERWISE `late: the court may allow a late claim if it considers it just, while the fund is not fully distributed (s 103W(4)); it has not yet done so`

-- s 103ZC(1) if the court makes an award of damages, a person who is or was a representative party or a sub-group
-- representative party may apply; (2) "If, on an application under this section, the court is satisfied the costs
-- reasonably incurred in relation to the representative proceeding by the applicant are likely to exceed the costs
-- recoverable by the applicant from the defendant, the court may order an amount equal to the whole or part of the
-- excess be paid to the applicant out of the damages awarded." The most is the whole excess. The two amounts are the
-- court's estimates ("likely"): asked. Where the conditions fail, no amount under s 103ZC: 0.
@export How much of the group's damages can the court order paid to the representative party to cover their unrecovered legal costs, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103ZC? At most the amount by which the costs they reasonably incurred are likely to exceed the costs they can recover from the defendant, and only if damages are awarded and the representative party (or a sub-group representative party) applies.
GIVEN `damages awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has made an award of damages in the representative proceeding
      `an application was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a person who is or was the representative party, or a sub-group representative party, has applied under s 103ZC
      `costs reasonably incurred` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs, in dollars, the applicant reasonably incurred in relation to the proceeding, as the court is likely to find them
      `costs recoverable` IS A NUMBER @desc The costs, in dollars, the applicant can recover from the defendant, as the court is likely to find them
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most paid out of the damages for the representative party's costs` MEANS
    IF `damages awarded` AND `an application was made` AND (`costs reasonably incurred` GREATER THAN `costs recoverable`)
    THEN `costs reasonably incurred` MINUS `costs recoverable`
    ELSE 0

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103M, 103N, 103ZB -- costs`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103ZB "In a representative proceeding, the court-- (a) may order a party to pay costs; but (b) may not order a group
-- member who is not a representative party to pay costs, other than under section 103M or 103N." s 103M(3) a
-- sub-group representative party (other than the representative party) "is liable for costs associated with deciding
-- the issue or issues common to the sub-group members"; s 103N(2) an individual group member allowed to appear "is
-- liable for costs associated with deciding the issue". A flat negative: JUST FALSE kind; "other than" met: the
-- liability those sections give (fork F11).
DECLARE `My role` IS ONE OF
    `the representative party`
    `a sub-group representative party appointed under s 103M`
    `a group member who is neither`

DECLARE `Can I be ordered to pay costs` IS ONE OF
    `yes: as the representative party you are a party, and the court may order you to pay costs (s 103ZB(a))`
    `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issues common to your sub-group, for which you, not the representative party, are liable (ss 103M(3), 103ZB(b))`
    `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issue that relates only to your claim, for which you, not the representative party, are liable (ss 103N(2), 103ZB(b))`
    `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issues common to your sub-group and of the issue that relates only to your claim (ss 103M(3), 103N(2), 103ZB(b))`
    `no: the court may not order a group member who is not a representative party to pay costs (s 103ZB(b))`

@export Can I be ordered to pay legal costs in a representative proceeding (class action), under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103ZB? The representative party can; an ordinary group member cannot, except for the costs of a sub-group issue they represent (s 103M) or of an individual issue they were allowed to appear on (s 103N).
GIVEN `role` IS A `My role` @desc Your role: the representative party; a sub-group representative party appointed by the court under s 103M; or a group member who is neither
      `appeared on my own issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court allowed you to appear in the proceeding to decide an issue that relates only to your own claim (s 103N)
GIVETH A `Can I be ordered to pay costs`
`Can I be ordered to pay costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `role`
    WHEN `the representative party` THEN `yes: as the representative party you are a party, and the court may order you to pay costs (s 103ZB(a))`
    WHEN `a sub-group representative party appointed under s 103M` THEN
        IF `appeared on my own issue`
        THEN `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issues common to your sub-group and of the issue that relates only to your claim (ss 103M(3), 103N(2), 103ZB(b))`
        ELSE `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issues common to your sub-group, for which you, not the representative party, are liable (ss 103M(3), 103ZB(b))`
    WHEN `a group member who is neither` THEN
        IF `appeared on my own issue`
        THEN `yes, but only the costs of deciding the issue that relates only to your claim, for which you, not the representative party, are liable (ss 103N(2), 103ZB(b))`
        ELSE `no: the court may not order a group member who is not a representative party to pay costs (s 103ZB(b))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103T, 103U -- notices to group members`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103T(1) notice "must be given" of (a) the start and the right to opt out, (b) a defendant's application to dismiss
-- for want of prosecution, (c) a representative party's application for leave to withdraw; (2) the court may dispense
-- with (1) "if the relief sought ... does not include a claim for damages"; (3) notice of a payment into court "if the
-- court orders"; (4) "Unless the court considers it just, an application for approval of a settlement under section
-- 103R must not be decided unless notice has been given"; (5) the court may order notice of any matter; (6) "as soon as
-- practicable after the happening of the event". Who gives it and how is for the court's order (s 103U(2)): not asked.
DECLARE `The matter` IS ONE OF
    `the start of the proceeding and my right to opt out`
    `the defendant's application to dismiss the proceeding for want of prosecution`
    `the representative party's application for leave to withdraw`
    `a payment into court of money in answer to a cause of action in the proceeding`
    `an application to approve a settlement`
    `any other matter`

DECLARE `Must I be given notice` IS ONE OF
    `yes: notice must be given to group members as soon as practicable after the event (s 103T(1), (6))`
    `no: the court has dispensed with the notice, as it may because the relief sought does not include damages (s 103T(2))`
    `yes: the court has ordered that notice be given, as soon as practicable after the event (s 103T(3), (5), (6))`
    `only if the court orders it (s 103T(3), (5))`
    `yes: the settlement must not be decided until notice has been given to group members (s 103T(4))`
    `no: the court considers it just to decide the settlement application without notice (s 103T(4))`

@export Must I, as a group member, be given notice of this step in the representative proceeding, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103T? Notice must be given of the start and the right to opt out, of a defendant's application to dismiss for want of prosecution, and of the representative party's application to withdraw (the court may dispense with these only where no damages are claimed); of a settlement before it is approved, unless the court considers it just to go without; and of anything else the court orders.
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `The matter` @desc The step or event the notice would be about
      `damages claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief sought in the representative proceeding includes a claim for damages
      `court dispensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has dispensed with the notice
      `court ordered notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered that notice of the matter be given to group members
      `court considers it just to go without` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a settlement: whether the court considers it just to decide the application for approval without notice to group members
GIVETH A `Must I be given notice`
`Must I be given notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `an application to approve a settlement` THEN
        IF `court considers it just to go without`
        THEN `no: the court considers it just to decide the settlement application without notice (s 103T(4))`
        ELSE `yes: the settlement must not be decided until notice has been given to group members (s 103T(4))`
    WHEN `a payment into court of money in answer to a cause of action in the proceeding` THEN
        IF `court ordered notice`
        THEN `yes: the court has ordered that notice be given, as soon as practicable after the event (s 103T(3), (5), (6))`
        ELSE `only if the court orders it (s 103T(3), (5))`
    WHEN `any other matter` THEN
        IF `court ordered notice`
        THEN `yes: the court has ordered that notice be given, as soon as practicable after the event (s 103T(3), (5), (6))`
        ELSE `only if the court orders it (s 103T(3), (5))`
    WHEN `the start of the proceeding and my right to opt out` THEN `s 103T(1), (2) -- notice` `damages claimed` `court dispensed`
    WHEN `the defendant's application to dismiss the proceeding for want of prosecution` THEN `s 103T(1), (2) -- notice` `damages claimed` `court dispensed`
    WHEN `the representative party's application for leave to withdraw` THEN `s 103T(1), (2) -- notice` `damages claimed` `court dispensed`

GIVEN `damages claimed` IS A BOOLEAN, `court dispensed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Must I be given notice`
`s 103T(1), (2) -- notice` `damages claimed` `court dispensed` MEANS
    IF `court dispensed` AND (NOT (`damages claimed`))
    THEN `no: the court has dispensed with the notice, as it may because the relief sought does not include damages (s 103T(2))`
    ELSE `yes: notice must be given to group members as soon as practicable after the event (s 103T(1), (6))`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103R, 103S, 103P -- settlement, and the representative party`
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103R(1) "A representative proceeding may not be settled or discontinued without the approval of the court." A flat
-- negative. (2) the court may order how settlement money is distributed.
@export Can the representative proceeding (class action) be settled or discontinued, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103R? Not without the court's approval; with it, the court may also order how the settlement money is shared among group members.
GIVEN `court approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has approved the settlement or discontinuance
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the proceeding be settled or discontinued` MEANS
    IF `court approved` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 103S(1) "A representative party may, with the leave of the court, settle the party's individual claim in whole or
-- part at any stage". A condition ("with the leave"): JUST FALSE without it (fork F12).
@export As the representative party, can I settle my own individual claim, in whole or part, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103S(1)? Only with the court's leave, but at any stage of the proceeding.
GIVEN `leave given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given you leave to settle your individual claim
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I settle my own claim as representative party` MEANS
    IF `leave given` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 103S(2) a representative party "seeking leave to settle, or who has settled, the party's individual claim may, with
-- leave of the court, withdraw as the representative party." (4) "Before a representative party may be granted leave to
-- withdraw ... (a) the court must be satisfied that notice of the application has been given to group members under
-- section 103T in sufficient time for a group member to apply under subsection (3) to have someone substituted as the
-- representative party; and (b) any application for the substitution of a group member as representative party must
-- have been decided." The first branch is a grant limited in its own words (fork F12).
DECLARE `Can I withdraw as representative party` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court has given you leave to withdraw (s 103S(2))`
    `possibly: the conditions in s 103S(4) are met, and the court may give you leave to withdraw (s 103S(2))`
    `not covered: s 103S(2) lets a representative party withdraw when seeking leave to settle, or having settled, their individual claim`
    `not yet: the court must first be satisfied that group members were told of your application in time to seek a substitute (s 103S(4)(a))`
    `not yet: any application to substitute a group member as representative party must be decided first (s 103S(4)(b))`

@export As the representative party, can I withdraw from that role, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103S(2) and (4)? When I am settling (or have settled) my own claim, with the court's leave, after group members have been told in time to seek a substitute, and after any application for a substitute is decided.
GIVEN `settling my own claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are seeking leave to settle, or have settled, your individual claim
      `notice given in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether notice of your application to withdraw was given to group members under s 103T in sufficient time for one of them to apply for a substitute (in the end the court's view)
      `substitution decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether every application to substitute a group member as representative party has been decided (answer yes if none was made)
      `leave given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has given you leave to withdraw
GIVETH A `Can I withdraw as representative party`
`Can I withdraw as representative party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`settling my own claim`)
        THEN `not covered: s 103S(2) lets a representative party withdraw when seeking leave to settle, or having settled, their individual claim`
        IF NOT (`notice given in time`)
        THEN `not yet: the court must first be satisfied that group members were told of your application in time to seek a substitute (s 103S(4)(a))`
        IF NOT (`substitution decided`)
        THEN `not yet: any application to substitute a group member as representative party must be decided first (s 103S(4)(b))`
        IF `leave given`
        THEN `yes: the court has given you leave to withdraw (s 103S(2))`
        OTHERWISE `possibly: the conditions in s 103S(4) are met, and the court may give you leave to withdraw (s 103S(2))`

-- s 103P(1) "If, on application by a group member, the court considers that a representative party is not able
-- adequately to represent the interests of the group members, the court may-- (a) substitute another group member as
-- the representative party". (2) the same for a sub-group member and the sub-group representative party. s 103S(3) when
-- the representative party seeks leave to withdraw, "the court may, on the application of a group member, make ... an
-- order for the substitution of a group member as the representative party" (no inadequacy needed).
DECLARE `Can the representative party be replaced` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute another group member as the representative party, because it considers the representative party cannot adequately represent the group (s 103P(1))`
    `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute another person as the sub-group representative party, because it considers that party cannot adequately represent the sub-group (s 103P(2))`
    `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute a group member as the representative party, because the representative party seeks leave to withdraw (s 103S(3))`
    `you may apply, but the court may substitute only if it considers the representative cannot adequately represent the group or sub-group (s 103P)`

DECLARE `Which representative` IS ONE OF
    `the representative party`
    `the representative party of my sub-group`

@export As a group member, can I ask the court to replace the representative party (or my sub-group's representative party), under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) ss 103P and 103S(3)? The court may substitute another if it considers the representative cannot adequately represent the group's interests, or, for the representative party, when they seek leave to withdraw.
GIVEN `which` IS A `Which representative` @desc Whose replacement you would ask for: the representative party, or the representative party of the sub-group you belong to
      `not adequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers that representative unable adequately to represent the interests of the group (or sub-group) members
      `withdrawing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative party is seeking the court's leave to withdraw as representative party (s 103S)
GIVETH A `Can the representative party be replaced`
`Can the representative party be replaced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which`
    WHEN `the representative party` THEN
        IF `not adequate`
        THEN `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute another group member as the representative party, because it considers the representative party cannot adequately represent the group (s 103P(1))`
        ELSE IF `withdrawing`
             THEN `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute a group member as the representative party, because the representative party seeks leave to withdraw (s 103S(3))`
             ELSE `you may apply, but the court may substitute only if it considers the representative cannot adequately represent the group or sub-group (s 103P)`
    WHEN `the representative party of my sub-group` THEN
        IF `not adequate`
        THEN `yes: you may apply, and the court may substitute another person as the sub-group representative party, because it considers that party cannot adequately represent the sub-group (s 103P(2))`
        ELSE `you may apply, but the court may substitute only if it considers the representative cannot adequately represent the group or sub-group (s 103P)`

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `ss 103I, 103J, 103K, 103L -- when the proceeding stops being a representative proceeding` -- situation: an
-- application, or the court's own motion, to end the representative form
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103I the court may order that the proceeding continue, or no longer continue, under Part 13A if "it appears likely
-- to the court that there are fewer than 7 group members". s 103J if the relief includes money for group members and,
-- on the defendant's application, the court considers the cost of identifying them and distributing would be excessive
-- having regard to the likely total: an order that it no longer continue, or a stay of the money relief. s 103K(1) on
-- the defendant's application or its own initiative, if it considers it in the interests of justice because of one of
-- (a)-(e); (2) it is not inappropriate under (e) "merely because" the group does not include everyone who might have
-- been included, or is aggregated for a purpose such as a litigation funding arrangement. Each is "may": the court's
-- view is asked, and the answer says what the court MAY do.
DECLARE `The s 103K ground` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `costs of continuing as a representative proceeding likely to exceed the costs of separate proceedings`
    `all the relief can be obtained by another kind of proceeding`
    `not an efficient and effective way of dealing with the claims`
    `the representative party cannot adequately represent the group members`
    `otherwise inappropriate, for a reason beyond the group's make-up or a funding arrangement`
    `otherwise inappropriate, merely because the group leaves out others or is aggregated for a funding arrangement`

DECLARE `Can it stop being a representative proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A (or that it continue), as it appears likely there are fewer than 7 group members (s 103I)`
    `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A, or stay the claim for money for group members, as distribution costs would be excessive (s 103J)`
    `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A, in the interests of justice (s 103K(1))`
    `no: none of ss 103I, 103J and 103K applies on these facts`

@export Can the court stop my class action continuing as a representative proceeding, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) ss 103I, 103J and 103K? It may if there are likely fewer than 7 group members, if the cost of finding group members and paying them out would be excessive, or if it is in the interests of justice on one of the grounds in s 103K (but not merely because the group leaves people out or was put together for a litigation funding arrangement).
GIVEN `fewer than 7 likely` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it appears likely to the court that there are fewer than 7 group members
      `money relief for members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the relief sought includes payment of money to group members (other than for costs)
      `distribution costs excessive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the defendant's application, the court considers the cost of identifying group members and distributing to them would be excessive given the likely total
      `the ground` IS A `The s 103K ground` @desc The ground, if any, on which the court considers it in the interests of justice that the proceeding no longer continue as a representative proceeding (choose "none" if none)
GIVETH A `Can it stop being a representative proceeding`
`Can the proceeding stop being a representative proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `fewer than 7 likely`
        THEN `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A (or that it continue), as it appears likely there are fewer than 7 group members (s 103I)`
        IF `money relief for members` AND `distribution costs excessive`
        THEN `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A, or stay the claim for money for group members, as distribution costs would be excessive (s 103J)`
        IF (`the ground` EQUALS `none`) OR (`the ground` EQUALS `otherwise inappropriate, merely because the group leaves out others or is aggregated for a funding arrangement`)
        THEN `no: none of ss 103I, 103J and 103K applies on these facts`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the court may order that it no longer continue under Part 13A, in the interests of justice (s 103K(1))`

-- s 103L "If the court makes an order under section 103I, 103J or 103K that a proceeding no longer continue under this
-- part-- (a) the proceeding may be continued as a proceeding by the representative party on the party's own behalf
-- against the defendant; and (b) on the application of a person who was a group member for the proceeding, the court
-- may order that the person be joined as an applicant or plaintiff in the continued proceeding."
DECLARE `After the order` IS ONE OF
    `you may continue the proceeding on your own behalf against the defendant (s 103L(a))`
    `you may apply to be joined as a plaintiff in the continued proceeding, and the court may order it (s 103L(b))`
    `not covered: s 103L applies after an order under s 103I, 103J or 103K that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A`

DECLARE `My role there` IS ONE OF
    `I am the representative party`
    `I am a group member`

@export The court has ordered that my class action no longer continue as a representative proceeding. What can I do, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103L? The representative party may carry it on for themselves; a group member may apply to be joined as a plaintiff.
GIVEN `order made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has ordered under s 103I, 103J or 103K that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A
      `role` IS A `My role there` @desc Whether you are the representative party or a group member
GIVETH A `After the order`
`What can I do after the proceeding stops being representative` MEANS
    IF NOT (`order made`)
    THEN `not covered: s 103L applies after an order under s 103I, 103J or 103K that the proceeding no longer continue under Part 13A`
    ELSE CONSIDER `role`
         WHEN `I am the representative party` THEN `you may continue the proceeding on your own behalf against the defendant (s 103L(a))`
         WHEN `I am a group member` THEN `you may apply to be joined as a plaintiff in the continued proceeding, and the court may order it (s 103L(b))`

-- s 103Q "If a defendant starts a proceeding in the court against a group member, the court may order a stay of
-- execution for any relief awarded to the group member in the representative proceeding until the other proceeding is
-- decided." Where the defendant has not sued the member in the court, the section is silent: NOTHING.
@export The defendant has started a separate proceeding against me in the Supreme Court. Can my share of what the class action awards be held back until that is decided, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103Q? The court may stay execution of the relief awarded to me until the other proceeding is decided.
GIVEN `defendant sued me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant has started a proceeding in the Supreme Court against you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my relief be held back` MEANS
    IF `defendant sued me` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- ===================================================================================================================
§§ `s 103Y -- appeals` -- situation: judgment has been given
-- ===================================================================================================================

-- s 103Y(3) "If a representative party or sub-group representative party does not start an appeal within the time for
-- starting the appeal, another member of the group or sub-group may, within a further 21 days, start an appeal on behalf
-- of the group members or sub-group members." The time for starting the appeal is set by rules of court (not this Act,
-- not deposited): its last day is asked. The rule: the representative party DOES start an appeal within its time, LEST I
-- may, within a further 21 days. The further 21 days run from the end of that last day (fork F13): the trace waits half
-- a day past it, so the LEST rule starts at the end of the last day.
GIVEN `the days for the representative party` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act done`
`s 103Y(3) -- an appeal by the representative party, or by me within a further 21 days` `the days for the representative party` MEANS
    PARTY `the representative party`
    DO `start an appeal`
    WITHIN `the days for the representative party`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `I`
        DO `start an appeal`
        WITHIN 21
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `I` BECAUSE "no appeal on behalf of the group within the further 21 days (s 103Y(3))"

GIVEN `the days for the representative party` IS A NUMBER, `the time I start` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 103Y(3) -- my appeal is in time` `the days for the representative party` `the time I start` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 103Y(3) -- an appeal by the representative party, or by me within a further 21 days` `the days for the representative party`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days for the representative party` PLUS 1/2)), (EVENT `I` `start an appeal` `the time I start`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Can I appeal for the group` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the representative party did not appeal in time, and you start an appeal on behalf of the group within the further 21 days (s 103Y(3))`
    `no: the further 21 days for a group member's appeal have passed (s 103Y(3))`
    `not yet: s 103Y(3) gives a group member a right to appeal once the representative party's time for appealing has passed without an appeal`
    `no need: the representative party has started an appeal, as representative of the group (s 103Y(2))`
    `not covered: s 103Y(3) lets a member of the group or sub-group appeal`

@export The representative party has not appealed the judgment. Can I start an appeal on behalf of the group (or my sub-group), under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103Y(3)? Another group member may start one within a further 21 days after the representative party's time for appealing ends.
GIVEN `a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of the group (or of the sub-group whose representative did not appeal)
      `the representative appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative party (or sub-group representative party) started an appeal within the time for starting it
      `the day the judgment was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the judgment was given (ISO 8601)
      `the last day for the representative` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time for the representative party to start an appeal, under the rules of court
      `the day I start` IS A DATE @desc The day you start, or plan to start, the appeal
GIVETH A `Can I appeal for the group`
`Can I appeal on behalf of the group` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a member`)
        THEN `not covered: s 103Y(3) lets a member of the group or sub-group appeal`
        IF `the representative appealed`
        THEN `no need: the representative party has started an appeal, as representative of the group (s 103Y(2))`
        IF `the day` `the day I start` `is on or before` `the last day for the representative`
        THEN `not yet: s 103Y(3) gives a group member a right to appeal once the representative party's time for appealing has passed without an appeal`
        IF `s 103Y(3) -- my appeal is in time` (`the days from` `the day the judgment was given` `to` `the last day for the representative`) (`the days from` `the day the judgment was given` `to` `the day I start`)
        THEN `yes: the representative party did not appeal in time, and you start an appeal on behalf of the group within the further 21 days (s 103Y(3))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the further 21 days for a group member's appeal have passed (s 103Y(3))`

@export By when must I start an appeal on behalf of the group if the representative party has not appealed, under the Civil Proceedings Act 2011 (Queensland) s 103Y(3)? Within a further 21 days after the representative party's time for appealing ends. No date is given if the representative party has appealed.
GIVEN `the representative appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the representative party (or sub-group representative party) started an appeal within the time for starting it
      `the last day for the representative` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the time for the representative party to start an appeal, under the rules of court (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I appeal on behalf of the group` MEANS
    IF `the representative appealed`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the day` 21 `days after` `the last day for the representative`)
